From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000013
Subject: [PATCH] @companion remove: delete the one companion named, and never with player gear on it

The row was deleted by name, and names are not unique (only shell_index is), so removing
one companion removed every one that shared its name. Delete by the shell_index the name
was resolved to instead.

Removing a companion also threw away any gear the player had given it. A summoned one now
hands that gear back first; one that is not summoned holds it only as a record, so it has
to be summoned and the gear taken back before it can be removed.

--- a/src/custom/atcommand.inc
+++ b/src/custom/atcommand.inc
@@ -430,12 +430,21 @@
 				break;
 			}
 		}
+		// Gear the player gave it is the player's: a summoned companion hands it back first, and
+		// one that is not summoned has it only as a record, so it has to be summoned for that.
+		if (live == nullptr && population_engine_companion_holds_given_gear(sd->status.account_id, index_)) {
+			char msg[NAME_LENGTH + 96];
+			snprintf(msg, sizeof(msg), "'%s' still has gear you gave it. Summon it and take it back with @companion gear first.", param);
+			clif_displaymessage(fd, msg);
+			return -1;
+		}
 		if (live != nullptr) {
+			population_engine_companion_return_gear(sd, live, 0);
 			if (live->status.party_id > 0 && live->status.party_id < 0x70000000)
 				population_engine_set_companion_active(sd->status.account_id, index_, false);
 			population_engine_shell_release(live);
 		}
-		if (population_engine_companion_delete(sd->status.account_id, param)) {
+		if (population_engine_companion_delete(sd->status.account_id, index_)) {
 			// The roster changed: let an open panel drop the row immediately.
 			population_engine_push_companion_list(sd);
 			char msg[NAME_LENGTH + 64];
